Date: Tue, 1 Sep 2026 16:26:28 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 003/105] feat: opt-in per-category FP8 for qwen4_exp dense
 path
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The NVFP4 checkpoint leaves the always-on dense modules (shared expert,
attention, linear-attention, hyper-connection mixers, gates, lm_head) in
BF16 — ~7.2GB of the ~9.8GB read per decoded token. This adds
--qwen4-exp-dense-fp8-categories to serve selected categories via the
existing FP8 linear method, quantized at load time. Default off; feature
off keeps the original compute paths (hyper-connection mixers only switch
off their fused path when quantized). The QSA indexer is hard-excluded
regardless of flags (a conservative choice: FP8 for the indexer's top-k
selection is not validated).

CPU-only tests: category routing, indexer guard, e4m3 quant-dequant bounds,
off-state parity of method selection. GPU validation checklist in docs.
Implemented by Codex (gpt-5.6-sol high) under supervisor review.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
